WEBVTT

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.400
<i>My name is Kiri.</i>

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.120
<i>The two things I despise above all 
else are laziness and negligence.</i>

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.330
<i>I believe that, in order to most 
efficiently achieve a goal,</i>

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.060
<i>strict discipline and a flawless 
plan are absolutely indispensable.</i>

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.260
<i>Indeed, my current goal is...</i>

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.140
<i>to get him back into his own bed.</i>

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.270
Victor! What are you doing in my bed?!

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:51.570
What am I doing? I'm reconfirming 
our father-son bond.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.330
Get out of my bed right now!

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.860
Okay, okay. What a cold son you are.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.040
Put on your underwear!

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.820
What's wrong? There's no need to be shy.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.080
This is your homeland, you know.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.750
Say that one more time, and I'll be 
"cutting" ties with my homeland.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.910
Jeez, you sure can't take a joke.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.040
<i>This is Victor.</i>

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>He's my lazy, negligent, and foolish father.</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.610
<i>We're on a journey to reclaim the 
time that's been taken from him.</i>

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.430
Why are you putting your socks 
on before your underwear?!

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.960
The casino town of C'est La Vie.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.790
People dazzled by lust for money 
flock to this town of greed.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.090
The greater the greed in a place, 
the more Horologues it attracts.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.510
Whoops, sorry.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:20.980
Hold it.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.910
Not a smart thing to do.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.970
I'll be taking my wallet back.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.810
S-Sorry, bro. I'll return it 
later with interest, okay?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.100
Give it back.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.900
I have a very sickly wife and a young son—

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.780
Give it back.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.740
Ah, so you're a father doing 
your best for your son, too?

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.020
I'm very concerned about my 
son's upbringing, as well.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.790
Huh? As young as you are?

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:52.020
That's right. So I very much 
understand how you feel.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.730
You can keep that money.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.250
H-Hey—

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.170
Th-Thank you!

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.190
Victor! That was our travel money!

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:02.780
What are you thinking,
giving it to that obvious lowlife?!

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:05.410
Relax and enjoy!

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.100
This is a casino town, isn't it?

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.920
I can win that kind of pocket 
change back in no time!

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.910
You think you're going 
to win it at a casino?!

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.150
Seriously, could he be any more frivolous?

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.610
Okay, I'm off.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:25.260
<i>He's always been like that.</i>

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.370
Why Won't You Stay With Us?

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.660
<i>Every time he went out, it was to gamble.</i>

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.010
<i>Honestly...</i>

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.870
<i>So this is how it feels to want 
to meet an unruly kid's parents.</i>

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.580
Please!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.060
I'm begging you!

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.480
A little more... Please,
 give me just a little more time!

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:02.030
I can't do that. Do you realize how 
accommodating I've been already?

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.400
But...

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.200
You have until 7:00 this 
evening to pay me back.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.450
I can't wait any longer than that.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:16.730
Why did I ever get into gambling?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.690
My wife and kid left me,

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.590
I lost my home and all my assets...

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.650
I never should have tried it.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:32.310
I wish I could go back to 
the past and start over.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.690
What are those things?!

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.570
M-Monsters!

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.200
Your regret drew Horologues here!

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.950
If you don't want to be eaten,
get out of here!

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:00.420
Now, then... This is the first time 
I've ever faced eight at once.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:02.870
But today will be an easy win.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.300
Because Victor isn't here to hold me back!

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:05.300
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.860
I control the time of water, 
making it my blade.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.300
Speed Up.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:45.300
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:49.070
Blade of a Thousand Lights

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.840
Blade of a Thousand Lights!

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:06.850
What's that?

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.620
A cloud? Smoke?

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.180
Maybe they're filming a movie?

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:19.200
<i>Victor and I have slain hundreds of 
Horologues in the past twelve years,</i>

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:22.960
<i>but I've never seen one this large.</i>

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.580
<i>If those last ones were in the 
300- or 400-year class,</i>

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.720
<i>these must be in a class of 
at least a few thousand.</i>

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:33.320
Help me...

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:33.320
I'll never gamble again!

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.970
If I'd known it would turn out like this...

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.970
I regret it all...

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.100
These people...

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.470
You idiots!

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.980
Stop! It's gonna devour your time!

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:54.530
Victor!

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.190
Even with the Oath of Time,

00:07:57.190 --> 00:08:00.270
I guess I can't completely stop 
the flow of time from inside me.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:01.290
What?!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.040
Why is this happening?!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.040
Don't panic, Kiri. It's simple.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.290
Basically...

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.270
All we need to do is get rid 
of this thing right now.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:20.040
Do those two belong to Chronos?

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:36.280
Speed Up!

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:37.160
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:43.750
Rain of a Thousand Camps!

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:43.750
Rain of a Thousand Camps

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.260
Maybe that wasn't enough water.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.020
Want me to give you some more?

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:55.010
Put that away.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.470
I remember you.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.250
It spoke?!

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.920
This is a town of greed 
and chaos, all right.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.390
Anything goes.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.400
It has been a long time, card user.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.400
You know me?

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.150
Of course I do.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:18.160
The one who devoured your 
time all those years ago...

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.740
was me.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.920
That's a huge Horologue!

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.670
Is Victor over there?

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.530
You ate my time?

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:37.510
That's right.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:43.090
That wound above your left 
breast was left after I dined.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:48.290
If that were not the case,
why would it resonate with me?

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.520
Resonate?

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.050
This really is my lucky day.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.660
To think I'd find the one I've 
wanted to see all this time!

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:56.740
Don't, Victor!

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.040
Speed Up!

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.820
Give me back my time!

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.680
Stop!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.530
Do you want to die?!

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.850
Speed Up accelerates the 
flow of time from you!

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:12.010
Your age will take a huge 
leap back all at once!

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:13.880
I don't care!

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.570
Twelve years of my life are riding on this!

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:19.630
Even if I can't get them back,
I will have revenge!

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:20.590
Revenge?

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.560
What's the point if you have 
to sacrifice yourself?!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.470
Having a falling-out, eh?

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.150
Humans truly are incomprehensible.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.200
That was no good at all.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.550
You're not using the Oath of Time
like you're supposed to.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:58.500
But I guess you always want 
to do things your own way.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.800
I'll give you three stars 
as a special service!

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:03.800
Who are you?

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.310
I missed you!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.180
Darling!

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:13.530
I'm your wife, Mina!

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:20.490
Oh, boy... Looks like we've got 
another pest on our hands.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.740
Time to go, Aiks.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.020
We don't want to create any more of a stir.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.080
We'll put Majesty in a bad mood.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:29.890
Stand down.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.550
Very well.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.290
It disappeared...

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:37.730
I guess they were filming 
a movie, after all.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.170
I'm gonna send this picture to my friend.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.630
That was pretty amazing, though.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.630
Oh, send it to me, too!

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:43.030
Victor, huh?

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.570
Where did the white Horologue go?!

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:59.600
It ran away, I guess.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.570
I almost didn't recognize you, though.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:04.280
You look so much younger, Victor.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.280
But you're as handsome as ever.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.700
I've missed you.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.910
Mina, I thank you for saving us.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.810
But please stop lying.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:17.870
Lying?

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.200
My mother's name was Nana.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:22.950
She left this life twelve years ago.

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:26.590
The name "Mina" has never 
appeared in Victor's journal.

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.350
Hmm... Nana?

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:32.100
So that's what I'm going to 
be called from now on, huh?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.020
Such a weird name.

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.390
<i>From now on?</i>

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:36.490
But I don't mind!

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:39.520
I've searched for so long, 
my beloved darling!

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:41.390
Even if you've forgotten,

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:44.650
we just need to start over 
from this first encounter!

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:48.940
Miss, I'm sorry, but I'm not in 
the right frame of mind now.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:49.450
Huh?

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:52.230
We've been searching all these years, too,

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:54.450
for the Horologue that devoured my time.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.120
And yet...

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:59.430
Just when I thought we finally 
found it, I let it escape!

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:03.050
Who am I supposed to take 
out this anger on?!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:05.050
Victor...

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:12.760
March 4th.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:14.970
I encountered the Horologue 
that devoured my time.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:16.330
But it got away.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:19.050
I'll take it out on Kiri to 
take my mind off my vexation.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.120
Hey, whoa!

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:23.240
I saw that coming, but still, 
you change gears too fast!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.900
Sheesh, you're so quick to anger.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:27.780
You need to take a more relaxed approach.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:31.110
What are you saying?! That was 
a once-in-a-lifetime chance!

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:34.670
It'll be fine. There'll be other chances.

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.480
What makes you so sure?!

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.360
Hmm... Intuition?

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:39.670
That's even worse!

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.670
Hey, don't mock intuition.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:44.980
You always ignore what's 
right in front of you!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:47.540
<i>I finally found him, and I'm the 
only one who's happy about it.</i>

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:50.800
<i>I guess I'm not even on 
his radar, after all.</i>

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.500
Wait! Victor's past is 
contained in that journal!

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.360
Give it back!

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.440
You'll just have to catch me, then.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:04.990
Stop!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.490
<i>There's no doubt about it. 
She's a Chronos Ruler!</i>

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.190
I have far too great a handicap right now,

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:16.200
so I'll teach you the correct 
way to use the Oath of Time.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:19.630
The Oath of Time has two powers.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.780
One is a power that can stop 
the outward flow of time,

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.700
even when a Horologue is nearby.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:28.120
But you can't get bitten 
like my darling was,

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:30.590
so you still need to be super 
careful around Horologues.

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:36.640
Its second power is to speed up 
or slow down objects around it.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.060
Speed Up!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.580
Sorry! Did that hurt?

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:48.940
My intermediary is wind.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:51.570
I can send anyone who gets in my way flying.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.800
I know all of that!

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.930
No, you don't know everything yet.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:57.500
What?

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.220
Watch closely.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:00.000
Slow Down!

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:00.000
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:02.580
Speed Up!

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:03.340
Great Kamaitachi

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:12.020
She slowed down air and solidified 
it into a blade of wind...

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:13.430
Bingo!

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.930
Impossible! You can't activate Speed 
Up while Slow Down is in effect!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:21.690
Victor and I can't activate Speed Up
and Slow Down simultaneously.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:22.730
Which means...

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:26.940
It means you don't yet know the 
true power of the Oath of Time.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:35.260
Would you return my journal, please?

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:37.290
It's more precious than my life.

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:40.290
And if I say I won't?

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:41.920
Well...

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:46.630
I'll **** and **** you, then **** until 
you ****, and then **** even if you ****.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.730
Victor, what are you saying?!

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.760
F-Fine! You can have it!

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.930
But I really don't get it.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.310
Why do you adhere to the past, darling?

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.720
Those memories aren't even yours.

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:00.500
What are you—

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.580
You believe that journal unconditionally.

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:07.610
About being bitten by the 
Horologue and everything else.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:14.720
But if you look at it another way,
doesn't that mean you have no memories left?

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:18.080
So can you really say 
it's something precious?

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:22.580
In that case...

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.290
Come build a future with me!

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:33.630
From now on, we'll live 
together, have fun together,

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:37.060
grieve together, and make 
wonderful memories together!

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:38.560
Okay, darling?

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:41.080
Darling?

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:43.850
You're right, Mina.

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:47.490
Still, I'm sorry, but I can't do that.

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:50.110
Why not? I'm your wife!

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.610
I'm sure many things happened in my life

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.360
before I was bitten by 
that Horologue at age 27.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.580
Even if it's not written in my journal...

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:02.360
Like ****ing with **** and 
****ing the **** so it ****...

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:04.500
Victor! What are you saying?!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:08.840
Do you think I can bear to not 
reclaim such fantastic memories?

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:10.660
I can't.

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:16.600
Plus, at a glance, you look 
younger than I am right now.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.160
So it's hard for me to 
believe you're my wife.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:20.970
The numbers don't add up.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.120
That's true...

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:28.440
You jerk!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.900
You jerk! You jerk! You jerk!

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:34.820
You're not the only one who 
was bitten by a Horologue!

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:44.170
Here, darling. Say, "Ah."

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.160
Ah...

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:47.960
It tastes like pure happiness, Mina.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.050
Call me "honey."

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.500
And don't forget the heart 
at the end of the sentence!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.440
Honey!

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:55.420
Darling, darling!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.150
Hey, you two!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:59.570
Give it a rest! You're in public!

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:00.670
Oh, dear.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:04.920
The virgin who's never even held a girl's 
hand is jealous of his hot daddy.

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.830
He'll never fall in love that way.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.130
I guess his virginity will just get worse
until he's a cranky old man who dies alone.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:12.060
As his mother, I'm concerned.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:13.490
Who said you're my mother?!

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:16.050
I don't need you worrying about my future!

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:19.820
Oh, my! Darling, why is our boy so contrary?

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.850
You can't blame him.
He's always been a troubled child.

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:25.790
I'll have to give him
some good, firm discipline!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:28.940
If he doesn't obey, we'll make 
him eat pasta through his nose.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.130
Nice idea, darling!

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.630
<i>This has doubled his attack power!</i>

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.920
Why are you so perfectly in sync?!

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.910
Didn't I tell you? I'm my darling's wife.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:43.180
When two people love each other, 
they start to think alike.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.060
What do I have to say 
to make you understand?

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:51.940
I look young because I was bitten by 
a Horologue, just like my darling.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.670
I'm not lying when I say I'm his wife.

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:58.590
You are lying. I saw my mother's dead body.

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:04.250
When time is reversed,
people revert from elders to children.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:07.450
So coming back from the dead 
isn't impossible, is it?

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.480
Also, at one time,

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:13.960
I was part of an organization called 
Chronos that fought Horologues.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:17.140
Hang on, Victor! You believe her?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:20.530
In the organization, my popularity 
was just as high as my scores!

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:24.620
She says I was hailed as the ace,
so it's undoubtedly true!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:27.180
You couldn't possibly be more conceited.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:28.900
It's not a lie.

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:34.630
I was my darling's partner. I know 
how he fought better than anyone.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:39.570
I'm sure there's still a record of his 
work at the Chronos headquarters.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.570
You can learn all the things in his past

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.210
that aren't in the journal 
if you look at them.

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.840
That includes information on 
the Horologue that bit him.

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.700
I'd like to confirm one thing.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:01.590
This "Chronos" organization 
really does exist, right?

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:04.580
You really are a doubter, aren't you?

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:08.100
I can forgive that, though.
That's what you call a mother's love.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:12.020
If this is some kind of trap, I swear...

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:16.070
That's the proof that Chronos exists.

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:19.360
It was Chronos that invented 
the Oath of Time.

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:23.010
The reason I can activate Speed Up
and Slow Down simultaneously

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:24.700
is because these are the latest technology.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:28.700
Also, your Oath of Time is an old model.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.560
But either way,
they're just mass-produced copies.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:34.600
There's also an original 
that these were based on.

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:35.540
Original?

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:39.440
The very first Oath of Time ever made.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:41.550
It's called "UNIQUE."

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:44.910
The one my darling has, 
the one and only UNIQUE,

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:49.850
is able to control the time of not 
only objects, but living things.

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:54.040
That's how he's able to avoid sudden, 
massive regressions in age.

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:55.560
You can't mean...

00:20:58.600 --> 00:20:59.320
Still,

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:03.050
if only one UNIQUE exists in the world,

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:05.660
then how are you keeping your 
own time from pouring out?

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.770
I'm back!

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:14.460
They said the soonest train 
departs tomorrow morning.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:15.630
Wait!

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:17.720
And as for this nosy little boy...

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:21.380
I guess I'll kill him.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:26.020
Darling! I missed you!

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:29.860
Sorry! I'll make up for making you wait.

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:35.730
Memory and Reminiscence

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:20.590
I'm sorry.

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:41.500
Twilight of the Idols
